From 8aeaf173fe1812f0da12485fc9af16d325274d86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:21:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 98/98] build-rootfs: skip sdm in the generic sbin build loop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The generic `for dir in sbin/*/` build loop ran `make -C sdm` with no CROSS
(it relies on each Makefile defaulting to the cross compiler; sdm's
CC=$(CROSS)gcc defaults to the host gcc) and runs before the contrib X stack
is staged — so when sgreet's objects were stale (X headers rebuilt) it tried
to host-compile sgreet and died "-march=i486 ... does not support x86-64".
sdm is already cross-built + installed separately, after the X stack, by the
dedicated block later in this file; skip it in the generic loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 build-rootfs.sh | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build-rootfs.sh b/build-rootfs.sh
index f0f1c90f..4e21f651 100755
--- a/build-rootfs.sh
+++ b/build-rootfs.sh
@@ -154,6 +154,11 @@ build_components() {
 
     echo "Building sbin (init, ld.so, ...)"
     for dir in "$TOP/sbin"/*/ ; do
+        # sdm (the display manager / sgreet Xlib client) needs the contrib X
+        # stack and is cross-built + installed separately below; this generic
+        # loop passes no CROSS, so sdm's Makefile (CC=$(CROSS)gcc) would fall
+        # back to the host gcc and fail "-march=i486 without -m32".  Skip it.
+        [ "$(basename "$dir")" = sdm ] && continue
         if [ -f "$dir/Makefile" ]; then
             make -C "$dir" -j4
         fi
